        "## Definition\n\nAssume the Axiom of Choice. Let $H$ be a complex Hilbert space and\n$\\mathcal B(H)$ the space of bounded linear operators on $H$\n([[def-space-of-bounded-linear-operators]]). For a set\n$\\mathcal S\\subseteq\\mathcal B(H)$, write\n\n$$\\mathcal S':=\\{T\\in\\mathcal B(H):Ts=sT\\text{ for every }s\\in\\mathcal S\\}, \\qquad \\mathcal S'':=(\\mathcal S')'.$$\n\nThe strong operator topology on $\\mathcal B(H)$ is the topology of pointwise\nnorm convergence: $T_\\alpha\\to T$ strongly exactly when\n$\\|(T_\\alpha-T)\\xi\\|\\to0$ for every $\\xi\\in H$. The weak operator topology is\nthe topology of pointwise matrix-coefficient convergence: $T_\\alpha\\to T$\nweakly exactly when $\\langle T_\\alpha\\xi,\\eta\\rangle\\to\\langle T\\xi,\\eta\\rangle$\nfor every $\\xi,\\eta\\in H$. Use the linear-first inner-product convention.\n\nA **concrete von Neumann algebra** on $H$ is a unital star subalgebra\n$M\\subseteq\\mathcal B(H)$ satisfying $M=M''$. Under Choice, the double\ncommutant theorem makes this equivalent to being closed in the weak operator\ntopology.\n\nAn operator $a\\in\\mathcal B(H)$ is **positive** when $a=a^*$ and\n$\\langle a\\xi,\\xi\\rangle\\ge0$ for every $\\xi\\in H$, using the bounded\nadjoint convention of [[thm-hilbert-adjoint-properties]]. Write $M_+$ for the\npositive operators in $M$ and $a\\le b$ when $b-a$ is positive.\n\nA vector $\\Omega\\in H$ is **cyclic** for $M$ when\n$\\overline{M\\Omega}=H$, and is **separating** for $M$ when\n$x\\Omega=0$ for $x\\in M$ implies $x=0$. For a unit vector $\\Omega$, define its\nvector functional by $\\omega_\\Omega(x)=\\langle x\\Omega,\\Omega\\rangle$.\nIt is **faithful** when $\\omega_\\Omega(x^*x)=0$ implies $x=0$; this is\nequivalent to $\\Omega$ being separating because\n$\\omega_\\Omega(x^*x)=\\|x\\Omega\\|^2$.\n\nFor a bounded linear functional $\\varphi:M\\to\\mathbb C$, **positive** means\n$\\varphi(a)\\ge0$ for every $a\\in M_+$. A positive functional is **normal**\nwhen $\\varphi(\\sup_\\alpha x_\\alpha)=\\sup_\\alpha\\varphi(x_\\alpha)$ for each\nbounded increasing net $(x_\\alpha)$ in $M_+$ whose supremum is taken in $M$."
      ],
      "def-qsmx-conjugate-hilbert-space-and-antilinear-adjoint": [
        null,
        "## Definition\n\nAssume Countable Choice. All inner products are linear in their first\nargument. If $H$ is a complex Hilbert space, its **conjugate Hilbert space**\n$\\overline H$ consists of symbols $\\overline x$ for $x\\in H$, with\n$\\overline x+\\overline y=\\overline{x+y}$,\n$a\\,\\overline x=\\overline{\\overline a\\,x}$ for $a\\in\\mathbb C$, and\n$$\\langle\\overline x,\\overline y\\rangle_{\\overline H} :=\\overline{\\langle x,y\\rangle_H}.$$\nThe canonical map $c_H:H\\to\\overline H$, $c_Hx=\\overline x$, is a\nconjugate-linear surjective isometry.\n\nFor complex Hilbert spaces $H_1,H_2$, a linear operator $A$ is a linear map\n$A:D(A)\\to H_2$ on a linear domain $D(A)\\subseteq H_1$. Its graph is\n$\\Gamma(A)=\\{(x,Ax):x\\in D(A)\\}\\subseteq H_1\\oplus H_2$, with the direct-sum\nHilbert norm. It is densely defined when $D(A)$ is dense in $H_1$, and closed\nwhen $\\Gamma(A)$ is closed.\n\nFor a densely defined linear operator $A:D(A)\\subseteq H_1\\to H_2$, define\n$D(A^*)$ to consist of those $y\\in H_2$ for which\n$x\\mapsto\\langle Ax,y\\rangle_{H_2}$ is bounded on $D(A)$ in the $H_1$ norm.\nThe bounded functional extends uniquely to $H_1$; its Riesz vector\n$A^*y\\in H_1$ is specified by\n$$\\langle Ax,y\\rangle_{H_2}=\\langle x,A^*y\\rangle_{H_1} \\qquad(x\\in D(A)).$$\nThis defines the linear adjoint $A^*:D(A^*)\\subseteq H_2\\to H_1$.\n\nAn operator $S:D(S)\\subseteq H\\to H$ is **antilinear** when\n$S(ax+by)=\\overline a\\,Sx+\\overline b\\,Sy$. Its associated linear operator\n$\\widetilde S:D(\\widetilde S)\\subseteq\\overline H\\to H$ is\n$D(\\widetilde S)=c_H(D(S))$ and\n$\\widetilde S(\\overline x)=Sx$. For densely defined antilinear $S$, define\n$$S^*:=c_H^{-1}\\widetilde S^*,$$\non the domain $D(S^*)=D(\\widetilde S^*)$. Thus $S^*$ is antilinear and\n$$\\langle Sx,y\\rangle_H=\\langle S^*y,x\\rangle_H \\qquad(x\\in D(S),\\ y\\in D(S^*)).$$"
      ],
      "lem-qsmx-trace-class-duality": [
        null,
        "## Statement\n\nAssume the Axiom of Choice. Let $H$ be a complex Hilbert space, and let\n$\\mathcal S_1(H)$ be its trace-class operators with trace norm $\\|\\cdot\\|_1$\nand trace $\\operatorname{Tr}$. Finite-rank operators are dense in\n$(\\mathcal S_1(H),\\|\\cdot\\|_1)$. For every bounded linear functional\n$\\Phi:\\mathcal S_1(H)\\to\\mathbb C$, there is a unique $X\\in\\mathcal B(H)$ such\nthat\n$$\\Phi(T)=\\operatorname{Tr}(TX)\\qquad(T\\in\\mathcal S_1(H)),$$\nand the correspondence is isometric:\n$\\|\\Phi\\|=\\|X\\|$."
      ],
      "lem-qsmx-linear-closed-polar-decomposition": [
        null,
        "## Statement\n\nAssume the Axiom of Choice. Let $H_1,H_2$ be complex Hilbert spaces and let\n$A:D(A)\\subseteq H_1\\to H_2$ be a linear operator with dense domain and closed\ngraph. Define $A^*$ as in the local Hilbert-space adjoint convention. Then\n$T:=A^*A$, on\n$D(T)=\\{x\\in D(A):Ax\\in D(A^*)\\}$, is positive and self-adjoint. Its positive\nsquare root $P:=T^{1/2}$ has domain $D(P)=D(A)$ and satisfies\n$\\|Px\\|=\\|Ax\\|$ for every $x\\in D(A)$. There is a unique partial isometry\n$U:H_1\\to H_2$ such that\n$$A=UP,\\qquad \\ker U=\\ker A.$$\nIts initial space is $\\overline{\\operatorname{ran}P}=(\\ker A)^\\perp$ and its\nfinal space is $\\overline{\\operatorname{ran}A}$. If $A$ is injective and has\ndense range, then $U$ is unitary."
      ],
      "lem-qsmx-bicommutant-and-commutant-cyclicity": [
        null,
        "## Statement\n\nAssume the Axiom of Choice. Let $H$ be a complex Hilbert space and let\n$R\\subseteq\\mathcal B(H)$ be a unital star subalgebra. Its strong-operator\nclosure is $R''$. If $M\\subseteq\\mathcal B(H)$ is a concrete von Neumann\nalgebra and $\\Omega\\in H$, then $\\Omega$ is cyclic for $M$ exactly when it is\nseparating for $M'$."
      ],
      "lem-qsmx-monotone-bounded-positive-net": [
        null,
        "## Statement\n\nAssume the Axiom of Choice. Let $H$ be a complex Hilbert space and\n$M\\subseteq\\mathcal B(H)$ a concrete von Neumann algebra. Let $I$ be a\nnonempty directed set, and let $(x_i)_{i\\in I}$ be a net in $M$ such that each\n$x_i$ is positive, $x_i\\le x_j$ whenever $i\\le j$, and\n$\\|x_i\\|\\le C$ for some finite $C\\ge0$. Here $A\\le B$ means that $A,B$ are\nself-adjoint and $\\langle A\\xi,\\xi\\rangle\\le\\langle B\\xi,\\xi\\rangle$ for every\n$\\xi\\in H$. Then the net has a least upper bound $x=\\sup_i x_i$ in $M_+$, and\n$x_i\\to x$ in the strong operator topology."
      ],
      "lem-qsmx-closed-antilinear-polar-calculus": [
        null,
        "## Statement\n\nAssume the Axiom of Choice. Let $H$ be a complex Hilbert space and let\n$S:D(S)\\subseteq H\\to H$ be a densely defined closable antilinear operator.\nIts graph closure $\\overline S$ is closed and has the polar decomposition\n$$\\overline S=J|\\overline S|,\\qquad |\\overline S|=(\\overline S^{\\,*}\\overline S)^{1/2}.$$\nHere $J$ is antilinear, vanishes on $\\ker\\overline S$, and is isometric on\n$(\\ker\\overline S)^\\perp$; if $\\overline S$ is injective and has dense range,\n$J$ is antiunitary.\n\nFor a concrete von Neumann algebra $M\\subseteq\\mathcal B(H)$ and a vector\n$\\Omega$ cyclic and separating for $M$, define\n$D(S_0)=M\\Omega$ and $S_0(x\\Omega)=x^*\\Omega$ for $x\\in M$. Then $S_0$ is\nwell defined, densely defined, antilinear, and closable."
      ],
      "lem-qsmx-von-neumann-predual": [
        null,
        "## Statement\n\nAssume the Axiom of Choice. Let $M\\subseteq\\mathcal B(H)$ be a concrete von\nNeumann algebra on a complex Hilbert space $H$, and define\n$$M_\\perp:=\\{T\\in\\mathcal S_1(H):\\operatorname{Tr}(Tx)=0 \\text{ for every }x\\in M\\}.$$\nEquip the coset space $Q:=\\mathcal S_1(H)/M_\\perp$ with the quotient norm.\nThen the trace pairing\n$$\\Psi:M\\to Q^*,\\qquad (\\Psi(x))([T])=\\operatorname{Tr}(Tx),$$\nis a well-defined isometric bijection, and $Q$ is a Banach space. Thus $Q$ is\nan isometric predual of $M$, and its dual unit ball is weak-star compact.\nEvery vector functional $x\\mapsto\\langle x\\xi,\\xi\\rangle$ and every positive\nfunctional in $Q$ preserves suprema of bounded increasing positive nets in\n$M$."
      ],
      "ex-qsmx-nonfaithful-gns-vector": [
        null,
        "## Statement\n\nAssume the Axiom of Choice. Let $n>1$, let $H=\\mathbb C^n$ with its standard\ninner product linear in the first argument, and let $M=\\mathcal B(H)=M_n(\\mathbb\nC)$ act on $H$ in its defining representation. Every nonzero vector in $H$ is\ncyclic for $M$, but no vector in $H$ is separating for $M$.\n\nNow let $\\rho\\in M$ be a faithful density matrix, meaning $\\rho=\\rho^*$,\n$\\langle\\rho v,v\\rangle>0$ for every nonzero $v\\in H$, and\n$\\operatorname{Tr}(\\rho)=1$. Let $K=M_n(\\mathbb C)$ with the\nHilbert–Schmidt inner product\n$$\\langle X,Y\\rangle_2:=\\operatorname{Tr}(Y^*X),$$\nand represent $M$ on $K$ by left multiplication $L_aX:=aX$. Then\n$\\{L_a:a\\in M\\}$ is a concrete von Neumann algebra on $K$, and\n$\\Omega:=\\rho^{1/2}$ is a unit cyclic and separating vector for this\nrepresentation. Its vector functional is\n$$\\langle L_a\\Omega,\\Omega\\rangle_2=\\operatorname{Tr}(\\rho a)\\qquad(a\\in M).$$"
      ]
    }
  }
}
